koronus-arrival-sender = Sector announcement
koronus-arrival-object-announcement = Attention! The Navis Nobilite report warp disturbances. A large unidentified object will soon arrive in the { $system } system. All vessels must exercise caution and prepare for combat.
koronus-arrival-tau-announcement = Attention! Augurs detect xenos aircraft controlled by Abominable Intelligence approaching the { $system } system. All vessels must immediately assume combat readiness!
koronus-arrival-command-description = Triggers an object or Tau drone group arrival, or displays event timers.
koronus-arrival-command-help = Usage: koronus_arrival [system [object|tau [map_path|easy|medium|hard [lifetime_seconds]]]]. Example: koronus_arrival Aivorius tau easy 120. A trailing number without a selector also sets lifetime. Lifetime starts on arrival; default is 20–30 minutes. With no arguments, shows remaining seconds for each event type. Only players in the arrival system and on its planets receive the announcement.
koronus-arrival-command-failed = Arrival could not start: check sector mode, system, map/group, lifetime (greater than 0 and at most 7200 seconds), and whether this event type is already pending or active.
koronus-arrival-command-started = { $system } / { $type }: arrival started. Arrival in { $seconds } s; departure { $lifetime } s after arrival.
koronus-arrival-command-status = { $system } / { $type }: next event in { $next } s; arrival in { $arrival } s; departure in { $departure } s. A dash means no active timer.
koronus-arrival-command-grid = Grid { $grid }: map { $map }, coordinates { $position }.
